### Result types — manual smoke test
#
# Runnable from IntelliJ (built in) or VS Code (REST Client extension).
# Run the token request first; the rest reuse the captured token.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   docker compose up -d          postgres, redis, kafka, keycloak, openfga
#   .\setup-keycloak.ps1          realm + testuser
#   .\setup-openfga.ps1           store + tuples for testuser
#   .\run-procedure-service.ps1   service on 8095
#
# @host points at the service directly, which is what these requests were
# verified against. Switch it to the gateway once the gateway has
# /api/v1/result-types/** in its Path= predicate — see the Gateway routing
# section of the service README.

@host = http://localhost:8095
# @host = http://localhost:8080
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180

### Get a token (run this first)
# @name token
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/sclera/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=sclera-app&username=testuser&password=testuser

> {% client.global.set("access_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### List — a freshly provisioned org has Fail (1) and Pass (2), both system types
GET {{host}}/api/v1/result-types
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### List only the active ones
GET {{host}}/api/v1/result-types?active=true
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### Create at an explicit rank — Amber slots in at 2 and pushes Pass to 3
# @name amber
POST {{host}}/api/v1/result-types
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "AMBER",
  "name": "Amber",
  "color": "#f39c12",
  "description": "Attention needed",
  "severityOrder": 2
}

> {% client.global.set("amber_id", response.body.data.id); %}

### Create without a rank — appends as least severe
POST {{host}}/api/v1/result-types
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
  "name": "Not applicable",
  "color": "#95a5a6",
  "description": "Question does not apply to this target"
}

### Rename and recolour — allowed, and reaches history: nothing snapshots these
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/result-types/{{amber_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Warning",
  "color": "#e67e22",
  "description": "Attention needed before the next inspection"
}

### Reorder — send every id in the org, most severe first
# Take the ids from the list response above.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/result-types/reorder
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderedIds": [
    "REPLACE_WITH_FAIL_ID",
    "REPLACE_WITH_AMBER_ID",
    "REPLACE_WITH_PASS_ID",
    "REPLACE_WITH_NOT_APPLICABLE_ID"
  ]
}

### Deactivate — hidden from list?active=true, still present unfiltered
POST {{host}}/api/v1/result-types/{{amber_id}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### Activate again
POST {{host}}/api/v1/result-types/{{amber_id}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### Delete a custom type — 204, and the remaining ranks close the gap
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/result-types/{{amber_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}


### ── Expected failures ────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Each of these should be refused. If one succeeds, something has regressed.

### Duplicate key → 409 CONFLICT
POST {{host}}/api/v1/result-types
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "key": "PASS", "name": "Duplicate", "color": "#123456" }

### Colour that is not six hex digits → 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{host}}/api/v1/result-types
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "key": "BAD_COLOUR", "name": "Bad", "color": "red" }

### Lower-case key → 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{host}}/api/v1/result-types
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "key": "lower", "name": "Lower", "color": "#123456" }

### Rank past the end of the list → 400, "must be between 1 and N"
POST {{host}}/api/v1/result-types
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "key": "TOO_FAR", "name": "Too far", "color": "#123456", "severityOrder": 99 }

### Delete a system type → 400, "Pass and Fail cannot be deleted"
# Substitute the id of PASS from the list response.
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/result-types/REPLACE_WITH_PASS_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### Deactivate a system type → 400, "Pass and Fail cannot be deactivated"
POST {{host}}/api/v1/result-types/REPLACE_WITH_FAIL_ID/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### Partial reorder list → 400, "must contain every result type"
POST {{host}}/api/v1/result-types/reorder
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderedIds": ["REPLACE_WITH_FAIL_ID"] }
